{"id":"prevedi-00-02-01-b","type":"prevedi","section":"00-02-01","title":"Gradi e radianti","minutes":2,"code":"import math\nprint(round(math.sin(math.radians(30)), 2))","codeHtml":"<span class=\"k\">import</span> math\n<span class=\"b\">print</span>(<span class=\"b\">round</span>(math.sin(math.radians(<span class=\"n\">30</span>)), <span class=\"n\">2</span>))","options":["0.5","-0.99","0.52","0.87"],"answer":0,"explain":"Le funzioni di <code>math</code> lavorano in <strong>radianti</strong>: convertendo 30° con <code>radians</code> si ottiene sin 30° = 0.5. Senza conversione <code>sin(30)</code> darebbe −0.99."}